# 🚀 Kubernetes Nodes Healthy But kubectl logs Is Blank

---

# Important Observation

Healthy nodes ≠ healthy logging pipeline.

---

# 🎯 Investigation Flow

```text id="m8im5z"
kubectl logs
      ↓
API Server
      ↓
kubelet
      ↓
container runtime
      ↓
container log files
```

---

# ✅ Step 1 — Check Pod Status

```bash id="0lbjns"
kubectl get pod
kubectl describe pod
```

---

# ✅ Step 2 — Validate Container Runtime

Possible issue:

* containerd logging broken
* Docker logging driver changed
* journald corruption

Check:

```bash id="v5o9wj"
crictl ps
crictl logs
```

---

# ✅ Step 3 — Verify Log File Existence

Kubernetes logs:

```text id="jlwm3m"
/var/log/pods/
/var/log/containers/
```

---

# ✅ Step 4 — Check kubelet

```bash id="p0qj9j"
journalctl -u kubelet
```

Possible:

* kubelet cannot read runtime logs
* CRI socket mismatch

---

# ✅ Step 5 — Runtime API Failure

Common production issue:

```text id="zb7uho"
containerd restarted
```

but kubelet stale CRI connection exists.

---

# 🎯 Most Likely Causes

| Cause                             | Result              |
| --------------------------------- | ------------------- |
| container runtime logging failure | blank logs          |
| log rotation corruption           | missing logs        |
| CRI mismatch                      | kubectl logs broken |
| ephemeral container crash         | no stdout retained  |

